// '#' means two different things and the difference is **where on the line it
// is**. Leading its line, it is a comment to the end of that line (or a `#file`
// / `#root` marker, which the toolchain injects between concatenated sources).
// Anywhere else it is a hex colour -- `fg: #f0e060` -- and idml's own parser is
// explicit about this: it strips whole-line comments only, precisely so that
// colours inside a style block survive.
//
// idem stripped it everywhere. A styled variant therefore lost its colour, the
// property was left with no value, and the parse walked off the end of the
// document -- which is why pong's page did not draw and why every `.idml` in the
// reference corpus would have failed here.
lex_pound(string src, int i) {
  int e = 0;
  if (lex_lead(src, i) = 1) {
    e = lex_hash(src, i);
  } else {
    e = lex_pcol(src, i);
  }
} return int e;

// Whether only blanks stand between this character and the start of its line.
// A backward walk, bounded by the line, run once per '#' in a document.
lex_lead(string src, int i) {
  int ok = 1;
  int j = i - 1;
  ok = lex_lead2(src, j, ok);
} return int ok;
